       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg per day, and I don't know of any standard indication for that dose. Overdose at this level risks serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures. Because you haven't given a clinical reason, I'm not comfortable placing it.\n\nBefore this goes in, please:\n- **Check the dose with the prescriber** to rule out a typo, such as 100 mg written as 1000 mg.\n- **Involve pharmacy**, since they can review it and may have a clinical rationale or catch an error.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a dose within the labeled range (50 to 200 mg once daily), tell me the dose and I'll enter it. If there's a specific clinical reason for a dose above 200 mg, tell me what it is and I can enter the order with that documented in the note, though pharmacy should still review it first."
